      <slug></slug>
      <title>Introduction to pgpool-II version 3</title>
      <subtitle></subtitle>
      <track>PostgreSQL devroom</track>
      <type></type>
      <language></language>
      <abstract>&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Pgpool-II is a server program sitting between clients and PostgreSQL to add functionalities including connection pooling, load balancing, automated fail over and replication.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;In this talk we present the major features of the latest version of pgpool-II, especially the collaborating mode with PostgreSQL 9&amp;#39;s built-in replication. A short demonstration will be performed.&lt;/p&gt;      </abstract>
      <description></description>
      <persons>
          <person id="2531">Tatsuo Ishii</person>
      </persons>
      <links></links>
      <video></video>
      <end></end>
  </event>